## Data

### NASA CEA thermodynamic and transport databases
- Paths: data/thermo.inp, data/trans.inp, data/thermo.lib, data/trans.lib
- Source/References: NASA TP-2002-211556: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/20020085330/downloads/20020085330.pdf

### NASA RP-1311 example inputs/outputs
- Paths: samples/*.inp, samples/*.out, source/bind/python/cea/samples/*.out
- Source/References: NASA RP-1311 Part 2: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19960044559/downloads/19960044559.pdf

cea-rs modifications (2026): Rust/Python validation, reactant support, rocket
expansion and packaging by Keplr contributors. This is not a NASA product.
The cea_rs.nasa compatibility layer is independently written over the Rust
bindings; NASA Python API names, signatures, constants and unit conventions
were inspected for interoperability. No NASA Python implementation was copied.
The text above is NASA's notice, kept unchanged. In this repository the NASA
databases are at vendor/thermo-species/data/thermo.inp and
vendor/nasa-transport/trans.inp. NASA example decks, original reference outputs,
and outputs generated by NASA CEA 3.3.4 are at tests/data/nasa/, with NASA's
unchanged NOTICE.txt copied as tests/data/nasa/NOTICE. The .lib files are not included.

